et\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2{sin}^{2}⁡{15}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266308 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12ff17ae-9319-5498-a5e0-1d49ddbef50a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Alternative Forms of Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71e998d5-b71a-5b7a-83f9-c951b357c51a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡{44}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266310} {:answer/id #uuid "cb7355d7-d4ac-596c-b658-aa7ab1696b00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{44}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266311} {:answer/id #uuid "a77c5fd7-c7a8-5284-b81b-43b64e7dba57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{44}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266312} {:answer/id #uuid "50788728-3e22-5641-a6d8-e147c1cebff2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{22}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{22}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266313} {:answer/id #uuid "7637427d-5809-525a-991c-8dd31755c894" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb7355d7-d4ac-596c-b658-aa7ab1696b00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{44}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266311} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc446ca9-dc6d-520f-97f6-9657373b913d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "69a7ca9e-fd71-55ad-91ce-07744b83a69e" :question/math-academy-id "q-7692" :question/problem "Express $2{cos}^{2}⁡{22}^{∘}-1$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={22}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{cos}^{2}⁡{22}^{∘}-1 & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\cdot {22}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡{44}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
